  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(76.02pt, 146.72pt, "Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, University of Wisconsin–Madison, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 167.42pt, "Madison, WI 53706, USA ")
  #line-at(72pt, 188.12pt, "*E-mail: chu.ma@wisc.edu ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 16.02pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 251.24pt, "Abstract ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 279.92pt, "Dynamic shaping of ultrasound into prescribed spatial patterns underlies a broad range of ")
  #line-at(72pt, 293.72pt, "biomedical and engineering applications. However, existing modulation strategies face ")
  #line-at(72pt, 307.52pt, "fundamental limitations: single element transducers paired with acoustic lenses lack ")
  #line-at(72pt, 321.32pt, "reconfigurability, whereas phased arrays require large numbers of independently driven elements, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 335.12pt, "leading to substantial hardware complexity, cost, and rigidity. Here we introduce a microfluidic ")
  #line-at(72pt, 348.92pt, "ultrasound lens system that enables reconfigurable spatial modulation of ultrasonic fields using ")
  #line-at(72pt, 362.72pt, "two orthogonal layers of soft microfluidic channels. Each channel is selectively filled with one of ")
  #line-at(72pt, 376.52pt, "two liquids with distinct sound speeds, such as water and silicone oil, via an FPGA controlled ")
  #line-at(72pt, 390.32pt, "array of micropumps, generating programmable binary phase patterns. Integrating a 20-row by 20-")
  #line-at(72pt, 404.12pt, "column microfluidic lens with a single element transducer, we demonstrate three-dimensional ")
  #line-at(72pt, 417.94pt, "ultrasound focusing with approximately 1 s reconfiguration time and spatial resolution comparable ")
  #line-at(72pt, 431.74pt, "to that of a 400-element transducer array. The system provides 400 addressable pixels through ")
  #line-at(72pt, 445.54pt, "parallel control of 80 pumps, allowing hardware complexity to scale with the square root of the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 459.34pt, "pixel count. Building on this platform, we demonstrate dynamic ultrasound heating with ")
  #line-at(72pt, 473.14pt, "reconfigurable spatial heating patterns, as well as remote particle manipulation. By integrating the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 486.94pt, "microfluidic lens with static holographic lenses, we achieve dynamically reconfigurable ")
  #line-at(72pt, 500.74pt, "ultrasound fields with enhanced spatial control. Furthermore, we demonstrate the versatile design ")
  #line-at(72pt, 514.54pt, "capabilities of the microfluidic lens platform through a cylindrical lens that manipulates ultrasound ")
  #line-at(72pt, 528.34pt, "propagation in the azimuthal direction. Owing to its liquid based, soft architecture, the microfluidic ")
  #line-at(72pt, 542.14pt, "lens offers design flexibility, scalable operation across ultrasound frequencies, low acoustic ")
  #line-at(72pt, 555.94pt, "transmission loss, and stable performance under high acoustic power. Together, these results ")
  #line-at(72pt, 569.74pt, "establish microfluidic phase modulation as a compact, scalable, and flexible approach for dynamic ")
  #line-at(72pt, 583.54pt, "ultrasound field control. ")
]

