  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(108.02pt, 83.22pt, "In the particle manipulation experiment (Fig. 4a), a cylindrical silicone‑rubber particle ")
  #line-at(72pt, 110.82pt, "(1.5 mm diameter, 1 mm height) was floated on the water surface, with the lens positioned 3 cm ")
  #line-at(72pt, 138.44pt, "below. Four liquid filling configurations were designed for the microfluidic channels, each ")
  #line-at(72pt, 166.04pt, "producing a focal spot at one corner of a square region on the water surface. As the filling patterns ")
  #line-at(72pt, 193.64pt, "switched sequentially, the acoustic focus moved accordingly, driving the particle to levitate ")
  #line-at(72pt, 221.24pt, "successively at the four corners of the square. ")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 248.84pt, "In the spatially selective heating experiment (Fig. 4b), a thermochromic film was ")
  #line-at(72pt, 276.44pt, "positioned 3 cm from the lens, with the film, lens, and transducer all immersed in water. The spatial ")
  #line-at(72pt, 304.04pt, "filling patterns were designed to focus the ultrasound generated by the transducer onto different ")
  #line-at(72pt, 331.64pt, "target locations on the thermochromic film. The transducer was driven at an input power of 1 W, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 359.24pt, "and each location was heated for 15 s, producing a clearly visible hot spot in the thermal images ")
  #line-at(72pt, 386.84pt, "captured by a thermal camera (FSFTOOLS, HP96), as shown in Supplementary Video 5. The ")
  #line-at(72pt, 414.46pt, "positions of individual heating points were designed to trace a “W”‑shaped pattern, as shown in ")
  #line-at(72pt, 442pt, "Fig. 4b. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 670.6pt, "Fig. 5 | Additional ultrasound shaping capabilities of the microfluidic lens. a.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(490.48pt, 670.6pt, " Dynamic ")
  #line-at(72pt, 691.32pt, "holographic field switching by combining a single‑layer microfluidic lens with a static hologram ")
  #line-at(72pt, 712.02pt, "lens. A liquid filling pattern of “101010101010101010” transforms the projected focal pattern ")
]

