// arXiv source page 12
#original-page(612pt, 792pt, (image("graphics/page-12.png", width: 10.5pt), 300.5pt, 756pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#4472c4"))
  #line-at(300.98pt, 765.48pt, "12 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 83.22pt, "a cylindrical piezoelectric transducer, enabling dynamic control of the polar ultrasound field ")
  #line-at(72pt, 110.82pt, "distribution. The microfluidic lens is placed around the cylindrical transducer. The ultrasound field ")
  #line-at(72pt, 138.44pt, "is characterized by scanning along a circular trajectory around the transducer (Supplementary ")
  #line-at(72pt, 166.04pt, "Note 7) at a distance of 10 mm from the outer surface of the microfluidic lens. When all channels ")
  #line-at(72pt, 193.64pt, "are filled with water, the emitted ultrasound field is approximately uniform in all directions. In ")
  #line-at(72pt, 221.24pt, "contrast, selectively filling a single channel with silicone oil while maintaining water in the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 248.84pt, "remaining channels concentrates acoustic energy toward the angular direction corresponding to ")
  #line-at(72pt, 276.44pt, "the oil-filled channel. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 16.02pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 325.76pt, "Summary and Discussion ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(108.02pt, 364.82pt, "In summary, we demonstrate a framework for reconfigurable microfluidic ultrasound ")
  #line-at(72pt, 392.42pt, "lenses with several key advantages over existing ultrasound modulation technologies, addressing ")
  #line-at(72pt, 420.04pt, "requirements shared by both biomedical and non-biomedical ultrasound systems. ")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 447.64pt, "The system enables dynamic reconfigurability using a single-element transducer, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 475.24pt, "eliminating the need for large multi-channel phased arrays. By selectively redistributing liquids ")
  #line-at(72pt, 502.84pt, "within a lens containing microfluidic channels, an unfocused single-element source is converted ")
  #line-at(72pt, 530.44pt, "into a programmable acoustic emitter capable of generating diverse spatial field patterns. This ")
  #line-at(72pt, 558.04pt, "approach substantially reduces system complexity, as the number of actively controlled elements ")
  #line-at(72pt, 585.64pt, "(i.e., micropumps) scales with the square root of the number of phase pixels rather than linearly. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 613.24pt, "As demonstrated by a 400-pixel lens driven by only 80 independently controlled micropumps, this ")
  #line-at(72pt, 640.84pt, "favorable scaling enables high spatial resolution without proportional increases in electronics, cost, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 668.44pt, "or power consumption. ")
]

// arXiv source page 13
#original-page(612pt, 792pt, (image("graphics/page-13.png", width: 10.5pt), 300.5pt, 756pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#4472c4"))
  #line-at(300.98pt, 765.48pt, "13 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(108.02pt, 83.22pt, "At the same time, the microfluidic lens offers high acoustic transmission efficiency, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 110.82pt, "mechanical compliance, and thermal robustness. Binary phase modulation implemented using two ")
  #line-at(72pt, 138.44pt, "liquids with similar acoustic impedance embedded in a soft matrix preserves ultrasound amplitude ")
  #line-at(72pt, 166.04pt, "while enabling effective wavefront control, minimizing energy losses commonly associated with ")
  #line-at(72pt, 193.64pt, "electronic or mechanically actuated modulation schemes. The soft, deformable architecture allows ")
  #line-at(72pt, 221.24pt, "conformal coupling to curved or irregular surfaces, while physical separation of the lens from ")
  #line-at(72pt, 248.84pt, "pumps and control electronics reduces acoustic scattering, impedance-matching constraints, and ")
  #line-at(72pt, 276.44pt, "heat generation during sustained high-power operation. ")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 304.04pt, "The platform further offers broad frequency and material scalability. The operating ")
  #line-at(72pt, 331.64pt, "frequency is determined primarily by the characteristic dimensions of the microfluidic channels ")
  #line-at(72pt, 359.24pt, "and can be adapted across a wide range of ultrasound frequencies using standard microfabrication ")
  #line-at(72pt, 386.84pt, "techniques. In addition to the liquids used here to demonstrate binary phase modulation, the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 414.46pt, "platform is compatible with a wide variety of fluids with distinct acoustic properties, enabling ")
  #line-at(72pt, 442pt, "flexible phase design and extension to more complex field structures.  ")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 469.6pt, "Finally, the presented microfluidic ultrasound lens is broadly applicable across a wide ")
  #line-at(72pt, 497.2pt, "spectrum of biomedical and non-biomedical ultrasound applications that share common ")
  #line-at(72pt, 524.8pt, "requirements for reconfigurable and spatially programmable acoustic fields. In biomedicine, the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 552.4pt, "platform is well suited for therapeutic modalities such as thermal ablation, histotripsy, lithotripsy, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 580pt, "and neuromodulation, where acoustic energy is delivered over milliseconds to seconds and focal ")
  #line-at(72pt, 607.6pt, "patterns are adjusted intermittently in response to treatment progression, tissue response, or target ")
  #line-at(72pt, 635.2pt, "repositioning. The conformal, soft architecture further supports use in transcranial ultrasound, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 662.8pt, "catheter-based or endoscopic ultrasound systems, and other anatomically constrained or wearable ")
  #line-at(72pt, 690.42pt, "configurations. Beyond biomedical contexts, the same capabilities are relevant to non-biomedical ")
]

// arXiv source page 14
#original-page(612pt, 792pt, (image("graphics/page-14.png", width: 10.5pt), 300.5pt, 756pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#4472c4"))
  #line-at(300.98pt, 765.48pt, "14 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 83.22pt, "ultrasound technologies, including acoustic manipulation and trapping, ultrasonic printing, energy ")
  #line-at(72pt, 110.82pt, "delivery, and robotic systems, where reconfigurable field control, compact form factor, and ")
  #line-at(72pt, 138.44pt, "reduced electronic channel count are critical. Together, these shared requirements position the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 166.04pt, "platform as a general solution for programmable ultrasound control across diverse application ")
  #line-at(72pt, 193.64pt, "domains. ")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 221.24pt, "Despite these advantages, the current implementation also highlights opportunities for ")
  #line-at(72pt, 248.84pt, "further improvement. The demonstrated pattern refresh time of approximately one second, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 276.44pt, "determined by the choice of liquids, channel dimensions, and pump characteristics, is well matched ")
  #line-at(72pt, 304.04pt, "to quasi-static applications mentioned above but can be further reduced through engineering ")
  #line-at(72pt, 331.64pt, "optimizations such as lower-viscosity fluids, increased pumping rates, or shorter fluidic paths. In ")
  #line-at(72pt, 359.24pt, "addition, while the present device is fabricated using multilayer soft-lithography, future adoption ")
  #line-at(72pt, 386.84pt, "of alternative fabrication strategies, including monolithic fabrication, bonding-free multilayer ")
  #line-at(72pt, 414.46pt, "processes, or additively manufactured enclosed microchannels, could enhance mechanical ")
  #line-at(72pt, 442pt, "robustness, reduce leakage risk, and improve long-term reliability. Addressing these challenges ")
  #line-at(72pt, 469.6pt, "will further expand the operational envelope and practical impact of microfluidic ultrasound lenses. ")
