// arXiv source page 27
#original-page(612pt, 792pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(303.48pt, 742.32pt, "8 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 83.16pt, "define the states of all 80 pumps in the array. These binary strings are decoded by the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 103.8pt, "microcontroller and transmitted via a modified SPI interface to two FPGA broads (DE0-Nano), ")
  #line-at(72pt, 124.56pt, "which wait for an external trigger pulse before updating all outputs simultaneously to ensure ")
  #line-at(72pt, 145.2pt, "synchronous switching. ")
  #line-at(108pt, 165.96pt, "Each FPGA controls 40 driver circuits, which are connected directly to the micropumps. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 186.6pt, "The driver circuit is a standard low-side switching configuration incorporating protection ")
  #line-at(72pt, 207.36pt, "components. A 1 kΩ series resistor is placed between each FPGA output pin and the MOSFET ")
  #line-at(72pt, 228pt, "gate to limit current flow to and from the FPGA. A flyback diode is connected in parallel with ")
  #line-at(72pt, 248.76pt, "each pump to suppress voltage spikes arising from the inductive load. When the MOSFET is ")
  #line-at(72pt, 269.4pt, "switched on, the output node is pulled low and the diode remains reverse-biased. Upon switch-off, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 290.16pt, "the flyback diode conducts transient currents, protecting the transistor from voltage surges. ")
  #line-at(108pt, 310.8pt, "The complete system provides parallel control of 80 micropumps operating over a voltage ")
  #line-at(72pt, 331.56pt, "range of 3.3 to 12 V, with individual pump currents ranging from 1 to 250 mA during operation. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 352.2pt, "To supply sufficient and stable power, three programmable power supplies (SPS-3010, Jesverty) ")
  #line-at(72pt, 372.96pt, "are connected in parallel. In this architecture, the FPGA controls pump switching, while the supply ")
  #line-at(72pt, 393.6pt, "voltage is set independently by the power sources. Higher drive voltages correspond to faster liquid ")
  #line-at(72pt, 414.36pt, "exchange within the microfluidic channels; however, to protect the microfluidic lens, the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 435pt, "maximum operating voltage is limited to 5 V. Under these conditions, full liquid pattern ")
  #line-at(72pt, 455.76pt, "reconfiguration across the lens is achieved in approximately 1 s. ")
]

