// arXiv source page 30
#original-page(612pt, 792pt, (image("graphics/page-30.png", width: 455.5pt), 76pt, 607pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(300.96pt, 742.32pt, "11 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 83.16pt, "integrity of the microfluidic lenses, we systematically evaluated the degree of swelling for the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 103.8pt, "lenses fabricated by different method by measuring the delamination time, which is the duration ")
  #line-at(72pt, 124.56pt, "required for the planar base layer to detach from the structured channel layer under continuous ")
  #line-at(72pt, 145.2pt, "exposure. A longer delamination time indicates superior resistance to swelling and enhanced ")
  #line-at(72pt, 165.96pt, "interfacial adhesion. ")
  #line-at(108pt, 186.6pt, "We first investigated the correlation between silicone oil viscosity and PDMS swelling. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 207.36pt, "The used PDMS samples (10:1 base-to-curing-agent ratio) were cured at 90 °C for 1 h, followed ")
  #line-at(72pt, 228pt, "by filling the channels with silicone oils of 1 cSt and 100 cSt. In the case of 1 cSt oil, delamination ")
  #line-at(72pt, 248.76pt, "occurred after 7 min, whereas no delamination was observed for 100 cSt oil even after 24 h. The ")
  #line-at(72pt, 269.4pt, "same experiment was repeated with PDMS cured at 130 °C overnight. Under these conditions, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 290.16pt, "delamination occurred after 20 min for 1 cSt oil, while no delamination was observed for 100 cSt ")
  #line-at(72pt, 310.8pt, "oil after 24 h. These results indicate that higher-viscosity silicone oil significantly reduces PDMS ")
  #line-at(72pt, 331.56pt, "swelling. However, considering the switching speed required for filling the liquid channels, 1 cSt ")
  #line-at(72pt, 352.2pt, "silicone oil was selected for subsequent experiments.  ")
