  #line-at(313.8pt, 127.32pt, "phase difference relative to the PDMS walls. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(108pt, 161.76pt, "In practice, several structural factors can influence the focusing performance of the acoustic ")
  #line-at(72pt, 182.4pt, "lens. The lens architecture requires internal walls to provide structural support and separate the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 203.16pt, "microfluidic channels. These walls may provide unfavorable wave scattering because of their ")
  #line-at(72pt, 223.8pt, "distinct acoustic properties with the needed infilling liquids. In this study, we characterized the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 244.56pt, "acoustic properties of the wall material, polydimethylsiloxane (PDMS) (refer to ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.977pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(461.28pt, 244.56pt, "Supplementary ")
  #line-at(72pt, 265.2pt, "Note 3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(105.84pt, 265.2pt, " for details). Our results indicate that PDMS exhibits an acoustic velocity comparable to ")
  #line-at(72pt, 285.96pt, "that of the silicone oils used. We subsequently simulated the impact of these internal walls on ")
  #line-at(72pt, 306.6pt, "ultrasound beam shaping. As shown in ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.977pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(274.08pt, 306.6pt, "Supplementary Fig. S15a")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(407.64pt, 306.6pt, ", we initially considered a ")
  #line-at(72pt, 327.36pt, "baseline pattern without walls, where the phase difference is generated solely by channels filled ")
  #line-at(72pt, 348.24pt, "with disparate liquids. The target focal distance of this pattern is ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(384.84pt, 348.24pt, "𝑧")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 8.504pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(390.36pt, 350.64pt, "଴")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(399.12pt, 348.24pt, "= 50")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(424.68pt, 348.24pt, " mm, characterized by a ")
  #line-at(72pt, 369.12pt, "well-defined focal spot. To quantify the influence of the walls, we recorded the peak intensity of ")
  #line-at(72pt, 390.12pt, "the baseline no-wall simulation at ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(242.64pt, 390.12pt, "𝑧= 50")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(277.56pt, 390.12pt, " mm,")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(302.28pt, 390.12pt, " 𝐼")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 8.504pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(308.64pt, 392.52pt, "௠௔௫")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(327.6pt, 390.12pt, ", and utilized it to normalize the simulated ")
  #line-at(72pt, 414.6pt, "field intensity for configurations containing walls: ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(316.56pt, 414.6pt, "𝐼")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 8.504pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(320.4pt, 417pt, "௡௢௥௠")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(344.04pt, 414.6pt, "(𝑥, 𝑦) =")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 8.504pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(387.72pt, 407.52pt, "ூ")
  #line-at(391.32pt, 407.52pt, "(")
  #line-at(394.8pt, 407.52pt, "௫")
  #line-at(400.08pt, 407.52pt, ",")
  #line-at(401.88pt, 407.52pt, "௬")
  #line-at(407.4pt, 407.52pt, ")")
  #line-at(389.64pt, 420.6pt, "ூ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.947pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(392.52pt, 422.28pt, "೘ೌೣ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(411pt, 414.6pt, ", ")
  #line-at(419.88pt, 414.6pt, "The normalized intensity ")
  #line-at(72pt, 440.88pt, "profiles, ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(114.6pt, 440.88pt, "𝐼")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 8.504pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(118.44pt, 443.28pt, "௡௢௥௠")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(142.08pt, 440.4pt, "(𝑥, 𝑦) ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(172.8pt, 440.88pt, "are presented in ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.977pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(253.56pt, 440.88pt, "Supplementary Figs. S15b–e")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(400.32pt, 440.88pt, ". The internal walls lead to a ")
  #line-at(72pt, 461.76pt, "reduction in peak intensity at the focal spot. Notably, the choice of infilling liquid plays a pivotal ")
  #line-at(72pt, 482.4pt, "role in maintaining performance: when the central channels are filled with silicone oil, which ")
  #line-at(72pt, 503.16pt, "closely matches the acoustic impedance and speed of PDMS, the lens demonstrates significantly ")
  #line-at(72pt, 523.8pt, "higher efficiency compared to configurations where the central channels are filled with water. The ")
  #line-at(72pt, 544.68pt, "same ultrasound field pattern can be produced by adding a constant ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(398.28pt, 544.68pt, "𝜋")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(405.6pt, 544.68pt, " phase shift to all the pixels. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 565.56pt, "Therefore, we should always choose the pattern distributions where the critical channels (e.g., the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 586.32pt, "central ones) are filled with silicone oil. ")
]

