  #line-at(72pt, 153.12pt, "7.2 Ultrasound field measurement for the cylindrical lens ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(108pt, 177.72pt, "The performance of the cylindrical lens was measured using a rotational scanning system. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 198.48pt, "A cylindrical transducer (SMC22D20H10412, STEMiNC Inc.) was placed at the center as the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 219.12pt, "acoustic source, while another transducer (V303-SU, Olympus Corp.) served as the receiver. The ")
  #line-at(72pt, 239.88pt, "cylindrical transducer is connected to the function generator and the power amplifier by dual ")
  #line-at(72pt, 260.52pt, "conductor wires, which is also covered by a clear epoxy resin layer to isolate it with water. Unlike ")
  #line-at(72pt, 281.28pt, "the linear scanning system where the sensor is moving to capture the signal, the cylindrical ")
  #line-at(72pt, 301.92pt, "transducer, integrated with the microfluidic lens, was mounted on a rotational mechanical stage, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 322.68pt, "while the sensing transducer remained stationary. During the rotation of the cylindrical transducer, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 343.32pt, "distance between the source and sensor was fixed at 10 mm.  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.977pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 372.12pt, "7.3 Dynamic acoustic particle manipulation ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(108pt, 396.72pt, "For dynamic acoustic manipulation of particles, the ultrasound transducer and the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 417.48pt, "microfluidic lens were immersed in water and oriented upward. A small silicone rubber particle ")
  #line-at(72pt, 438.12pt, "(cylindrical, 1.5 mm in diameter and 1 mm in height) was placed on the water surface. When the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 458.88pt, "transducer was turned on, the particle was trapped at the acoustic focal spot. By dynamically ")
  #line-at(72pt, 479.52pt, "reconfiguring the liquid filling patterns in the microfluidic lens to shift the focal spot position, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 500.28pt, "the particle could be controllably levitated at different position across the water surface. ")
]

